# Optional settings for `docker compose` (docker-compose.yml). Copy this file to .env to use it;
# Compose reads .env from this directory on its own. Every line below shows the default, except
# the lines that switch the model (profile, provider, temperature and the endpoint example), which
# show a value to set; the stack runs without a .env at all. This file is not read by the console
# or by `uv run`; the console's own setting is web/.env.example.
#
# Never put a secret in a file you commit. .env is git-ignored; this example is not.

# Host ports. Both are published on 127.0.0.1 only (demo mode has no password).
# API_PORT is built into the console image (it is the URL the browser calls), so after changing
# it run `make up` or `docker compose up -d --build` to rebuild.
#API_PORT=8000
#WEB_PORT=3000

# Host names the API answers to besides localhost, 127.0.0.1 and [::1] (always accepted, any port),
# comma-separated, names only. Demo mode refuses a request whose Host header is any other name, so
# a page that points its own name at 127.0.0.1 cannot sign in as an admin; list the name you reach
# the API by if it is not one of those. Set outside demo mode, the same list is enforced there.
#TWOTRACK_ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# ---- Local model through the bundled Ollama -------------------------------------------------
# `make up-ollama` does all of this for one run. To make it the default for this checkout, set:
#
#   COMPOSE_PROFILES=ollama        starts the ollama and ollama-pull services
#   TWOTRACK_PROVIDER=openai_compat   points the API at a real model (default: mock, no key)
#
# `--profile ollama` on the command line adds the same services, but only TWOTRACK_PROVIDER
# switches the API (Compose profiles cannot change another service's settings), so use both.
#COMPOSE_PROFILES=ollama
#TWOTRACK_PROVIDER=openai_compat

# The model the ollama profile pulls and the API asks for. A small one so the first start is
# quick on a laptop CPU; any model name from https://ollama.com/library works.
#OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:0.5b

# How long the API waits for a model, in seconds: for an answer, and for its routing opinion.
# When a call outlasts its timeout the question is still answered, but without the model (rule
# routing, template narration). The API's own defaults are 30 and 10, which a model on the CPU
# inside Docker does not meet (a model on a CPU is far slower than a hosted one), so
# the compose file defaults to the values below. Lower them for a fast endpoint (a GPU, or a
# hosted model), raise them for a bigger OLLAMA_MODEL; a malformed value stops the API at start-up.
#TWOTRACK_LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
#TWOTRACK_LLM_ROUTE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=90

# The temperature the API sends. Unset (or empty): each call's own (routing 0, narration 0.2,
# chat 0.3, agent steps 0). A number from 0 to 2: that value for every call. "omit": none at all.
# Some models reject a non-default temperature; set TWOTRACK_LLM_TEMPERATURE=omit to leave it out of requests.
#TWOTRACK_LLM_TEMPERATURE=omit

# ---- Another model endpoint (no profile needed) ---------------------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint that needs no key, for example Ollama running natively on the
# host (on a Mac this can use the GPU, unlike the container). An endpoint that needs a key is
# configured in docker-compose.override.yml, not here.
#TWOTRACK_PROVIDER=openai_compat
#TWOTRACK_LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
#TWOTRACK_LLM_MODEL=llama3.2

# ---- Exploration runtime (the open_task route) ----------------------------------------------
# Compose: the API image carries Node and the Pi worker, and docker-compose.yml fixes
# TWOTRACK_ALLOW_OPEN_TASK=1 and TWOTRACK_EXPLORER=pi on the api service. A line here does not
# change those two (a docker-compose.override.yml does); it does set every TWOTRACK_EXPLORE_*
# setting below (the budgets, the tool allowlist and the worker's start-up timeout; unset or
# empty keeps the API's default), and `make smoke` checks that a question no report covers runs
# in Pi on the mock model. The image also sets TWOTRACK_PI_HARNESS_DIR. The rest of this section
# is for running the API yourself (`uv run twotrack serve`): it reads these from the shell, and
# needs TWOTRACK_ALLOW_OPEN_TASK=1 there to turn the route on.
#
# Which runtime plans an open task: builtin (no Node needed) or pi (Pi's agent loop in a
# restricted Node worker; needs Node 22.19 or newer and `npm ci --ignore-scripts` in
# harness/pi). With pi, a missing Node or worker, or packages other than the pinned ones, stop
# the API at start-up; nothing falls back to builtin.
#TWOTRACK_EXPLORER=builtin
# The worker's directory, when it is not harness/pi of this checkout.
#TWOTRACK_PI_HARNESS_DIR=
# The budgets of one run, for either runtime: model turns, tool calls the model asks for
# (refused ones count), and the run's wall clock in seconds. A spent turn or call budget stops
# the run with that reason; a run past its clock is a failure. The last one is for pi only: how
# long the worker waits for the API to answer one tool call, in seconds.
#TWOTRACK_EXPLORE_MAX_TURNS=4
#TWOTRACK_EXPLORE_MAX_CALLS=6
#TWOTRACK_EXPLORE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
#TWOTRACK_EXPLORE_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
# What a run may offer the model, for either runtime: comma-separated tool or workflow names.
# Only targets whose plugin declares explorable=True are ever offered, and only those the user's
# roles allow. Unset, every such target is offered except external ones (calls that send data
# out of the deployment): an external target is offered only when named here, and each of its
# calls still waits for a person's approval. A name that is not an explorable tool or workflow
# stops the API at start-up.
#TWOTRACK_EXPLORE_TOOLS=
# For pi only: how long the worker may take to start (Node plus Pi, until it says hello), in
# seconds. The run's wall clock above starts after that, so a slow start never eats the run's
# budget; a worker that is not up in time ends the run as worker_unavailable.
#TWOTRACK_EXPLORE_STARTUP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=20
# The model pi talks to: with TWOTRACK_PROVIDER=openai_compat, the TWOTRACK_LLM_* endpoint
# (TWOTRACK_LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS bounds each request; no temperature is sent, whatever
# TWOTRACK_LLM_TEMPERATURE says; a key reaches the worker only through its environment). When no
# TWOTRACK_LLM_* model is configured it is the mock model, served by the API on 127.0.0.1 for
# each run, so no key is needed.
